static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3463160Z     	
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3463546Z     		"gitlab-mr-commit"
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3464149Z     			Same as gitlab-mr-discussion, but report results to GitLab comments for
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3464799Z     			each commits in Merge Requests.
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3465263Z     	
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3465659Z     		"gerrit-change-review"
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3466165Z     			Report results to Gerrit Change comments.
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3466928Z     	
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3467481Z     			1. Set GERRIT_USERNAME and GERRIT_PASSWORD for basic authentication or
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3468192Z     			GIT_GITCOOKIE_PATH for git cookie based authentication.
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3468926Z     			2. Set GERRIT_CHANGE_ID, GERRIT_REVISION_ID GERRIT_BRANCH and GERRIT_ADDRESS
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3469527Z     	
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3469904Z     			For example:
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3470429Z     				$ export GERRIT_CHANGE_ID=myproject~master~I1293efab014de2
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3471033Z     				$ export GERRIT_REVISION_ID=ed318bf9a3c
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3471570Z     				$ export GERRIT_BRANCH=master
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3472161Z     				$ export GERRIT_ADDRESS=http://localhost:8080
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3472661Z     	
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3473066Z     		"bitbucket-code-report"
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3473598Z     			Create Bitbucket Code Report via Code Insights
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3474283Z     			(https://confluence.atlassian.com/display/BITBUCKET/Code+insights).
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3474938Z     			You can set custom report name with:
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3475407Z     	
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3475992Z     			If running as part of Bitbucket Pipelines no additional configurations is needed.
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3477196Z     			If running outside of Bitbucket Pipelines you need to provide git repo data
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3477997Z     			(see documentation below for local reporters) and BitBucket credentials:
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3478713Z     			- For Basic Auth you need to set following env variables:
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3479310Z     				  BITBUCKET_USER and BITBUCKET_PASSWORD
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3479922Z     			- For AccessToken Auth you need to set BITBUCKET_ACCESS_TOKEN
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3480472Z     	
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3481000Z     			To post results to Bitbucket Server specify BITBUCKET_SERVER_URL.
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3481730Z     	
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3482144Z     		"gitea-pr-review"
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3482627Z     			Report results to Gitea review comments.
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3483111Z     	
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3483583Z     			1. Set REVIEWDOG_GITEA_API_TOKEN environment variable.
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3484456Z     			Go to https://<gitea-server>/user/settings/applications and create new Access Token token with repo scope.
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3485391Z     			2. Set GITEA_ADDRESS environment variable to your Gitea server base address.
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3486011Z     			For example:
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3486721Z     				$ export GITEA_ADDRESS=http://localhost:3000
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3487231Z     	
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3487714Z     		For GitHub Enterprise and self hosted GitLab or Gitea, set
static / reviewdog (diff-only)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-26T11:39:46.3488509Z     		REVIEWDOG_INSECURE_SKIP_VERIFY to skip verifying SSL (please use this at your own risk)
